    <!-- Interrogative Pronouns (OLiA: InterrogativePronoun)
         Per Huddleston & Pullum (2002) *Cambridge Grammar of the English
         Language* §5.5 — the closed set of wh-interrogative pronouns
         in English. -->
    <!-- The interrogative class rides each Sense's `subcat` as its OLiA
         Reference-Model fragment (the universal grammatical-class identity); the
         category is DERIVED from that class by the loaded OLiA→CCG functor
         (lambek::category_projection), never per word here. Ambiguous wh-words
         carry multiple entries (which/what are pronoun AND determiner; when is
         this interrogative adverb AND the subordinator below) — the chart
         explores all. H&P (2002) Ch.5 §5 (pronouns/determiners) + Ch.7 (adverbs). -->
    <!-- Interrogative pronouns (OLiA: InterrogativePronoun). Each carries a
         DISTINCT synset (not a shared `fw-interrogative-pron`) so the
         praxis-side `wh_referent_role_from_synset` codec can decode the
         "expected answer type" feature — Cysouw (2004) "Interrogative
         words: an exercise in lexical typology", handout, session on
         question formation in Bantu, ZAS Berlin, 13 Feb 2004, §3.2 table
         (9): who/whom → PERSON, what → THING, which → SELECTION. The
         `subcat` stays the shared OLiA `InterrogativePronoun` fragment
         (unaffected — the CCG category projection is orthogonal to this
         feature). -->
    <LexicalEntry id="fw-what"><Lemma writtenForm="what" partOfSpeech="pron"/><Sense id="fw-what-1" synset="fw-interrogative-pron-thing" subcat="InterrogativePronoun"/></LexicalEntry>
    <LexicalEntry id="fw-who"><Lemma writtenForm="who" partOfSpeech="pron"/><Sense id="fw-who-1" synset="fw-interrogative-pron-person" subcat="InterrogativePronoun"/></LexicalEntry>
    <LexicalEntry id="fw-which"><Lemma writtenForm="which" partOfSpeech="pron"/><Sense id="fw-which-1" synset="fw-interrogative-pron-selection" subcat="InterrogativePronoun"/></LexicalEntry>
    <LexicalEntry id="fw-whom"><Lemma writtenForm="whom" partOfSpeech="pron"/><Sense id="fw-whom-1" synset="fw-interrogative-pron-person" subcat="InterrogativePronoun"/></LexicalEntry>
    <!-- Interrogative determiners (OLiA: InterrogativeDeterminer) — "which dog", "what time", "whose book". Same Cysouw (2004) §3.2 table (9) role split as the pronouns above (the SAME lexical item realized as a determiner rather than heading its own NP): what→THING, which→SELECTION, whose→PERSON (possessor). -->
    <LexicalEntry id="fw-which-det"><Lemma writtenForm="which" partOfSpeech="det"/><Sense id="fw-which-det-1" synset="fw-interrogative-det-selection" subcat="InterrogativeDeterminer"/></LexicalEntry>
    <LexicalEntry id="fw-what-det"><Lemma writtenForm="what" partOfSpeech="det"/><Sense id="fw-what-det-1" synset="fw-interrogative-det-thing" subcat="InterrogativeDeterminer"/></LexicalEntry>
